        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "Every JSON write now needs a writable `REFLEX_DIR`. Before, it needed only a writable `.web`.\n\nI tested `update_json_file` with `REFLEX_DIR` set to a read-only directory (mode 555). On `main` the writ"
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "This adds `filelock` as a new hard runtime dependency of `reflex`. Today it comes only through dev dependencies (virtualenv, pytest-split). The floor is also the newest release.\n\nThe race is between c"
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "This calls the private `path_ops._json_file_lock` from another module. Please expose one helper in `path_ops` (for example, a context manager that locks the JSON files of a directory) and call that he"
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "`reflex/constants/base.py` only re-exports `reflex_base`. This constant also goes into `reflex.constants.__all__`, so it becomes public API. Please make it a private module constant in `path_ops`, whi"
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "The names have 64 random bits, and `O_EXCL` already catches a collision. One attempt is sufficient. Please remove the 100-iteration loop and its `else` branch."
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "`fp` is resolved here, and `_json_file_lock_path` resolves it again. The callers in `frontend_skeleton.py` also resolve before they call `_json_file_lock`. Please resolve once, at the entry point."
      }
    ]
